# Ordering: the result of a three-way comparison. `less` means the left value sorts before the right, `greater` after, `equal` the same. It is the currency type every comparator and ordered structure returns. The named predicates and `reverse` read off the case; `from-numbers` is the base comparator the rest build on.

form ordering
  case less
  case equal
  case greater

  task is-less
    take self
    like boolean
    fork case, read self
      case less
        send back, wave true
      case equal
        send back, wave false
      case greater
        send back, wave false

  task is-equal
    take self
    like boolean
    fork case, read self
      case equal
        send back, wave true
      case less
        send back, wave false
      case greater
        send back, wave false

  task is-greater
    take self
    like boolean
    fork case, read self
      case greater
        send back, wave true
      case less
        send back, wave false
      case equal
        send back, wave false

  # flip the direction: less becomes greater, greater becomes less, equal stays. Turns an ascending comparator into a descending one.
  task reverse
    take self
    like ordering
    fork case, read self
      case less
        send back, make greater
      case equal
        send back, make equal
      case greater
        send back, make less

# the base numeric comparator: -1 / 0 / +1 as the three cases. Every other comparator and sort builds on this.
task from-numbers
  take left, like number
  take right, like number
  like ordering
  fork test
    hook test
      call is-below
        read left
        read right
    hook hold
      send back, make less
    hook miss
      fork test
        hook test
          call is-above
            read left
            read right
        hook hold
          send back, make greater
        hook miss
          send back, make equal
